# What must never enter the build context. The reasoning is the backend's, in
# the file next door: a fat context is slow to send to the daemon, and host
# state copied into the image quietly overrides what the image built for
# itself.

# Installed by the image itself, from the lock file, for the right platform.
# It is also the single largest directory in this repository, so leaving it out
# is most of the difference between a context measured in megabytes and one
# measured in hundreds.
node_modules/

# The bundle the image builds for itself. A stale one from the host is the
# worst possible thing to ship: it looks like a build and is a memory.
dist/

# Tool output that means nothing inside the image.
coverage/

# Local overrides. The container is configured by compose, not by these — and
# here the omission would bite harder than it does next door: Vite reads
# .env.local itself during `npm run build`, so a developer's own VITE_API_URL
# would be frozen into a production bundle without the build saying a word.
.env
.env.*

# Reserved for Playwright and empty (ticket 24). The runtime image serves
# static files; it does not drive a browser.
e2e/

# Not part of the application.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
